  },
  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 20 May 1964 and declared the next day: three aldermen (for six years) and twelve councillors. Of the fifteen members of the new council fourteen were Unionists; Thomas Newell (Labour) beat Ralph O'Lone in the four-man contest for the three aldermanships. Percentage poll: 51.44 (aldermen), 65 (councillors). All twelve Unionist candidates were elected, Dr George Dougan (a newcomer) topping the poll. Strain and Bone stood as Labour (Northern Ireland Labour Party, as in 1958 and 1961); McClatchey's label is not given in the results box."
}
